WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.625 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.670 line:84%
HANSON: American
citizens are threatened

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.250 line:84%
by the loss of
their middle class,

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.650 line:84%
by the loss of their
sovereign borders,

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.860 line:84%
and especially from elites
of an administrative state

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.570 line:84%
and globalism that
would surrender

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.079 line:84%
our sovereignty to an
unknown body of world experts

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:17.190 line:90%
or technocrats.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.440 line:84%
There are two million
people scheduled

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.840 line:84%
to cross the borders
of the United States

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.940 line:90%
between Mexico and America.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.520 line:84%
None of them are going
to enter legally,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.830 line:84%
no vaccinations
for COVID; there's

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.050 line:84%
going to be no test
for COVID, solely

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.140 line:84%
for the purpose of enhancing
the Progressive agenda

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.480 line:90%
and the Democratic Party.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.420 line:84%
We have no border, and
there is no immigration law.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.550 line:84%
If we look, more importantly,
at the middle class,

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.990 line:84%
we are emerging from a
pandemic, a population

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.950 line:84%
emerging from quarantine, an
already inflationary cycle,

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.340 line:84%
where we were not producing
goods and services because

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.350 line:84%
of the quarantine,
or the population

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.360 line:84%
was not growing in a
vast rate that would

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.190 line:90%
justify printing more money.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.570 line:90%
And yet that's what we're doing.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.930 line:84%
And the result of it is, for
the first time in 30 years,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.800 line:84%
we have an annual inflation
rate of somewhere between 4.5%

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.880 line:90%
to 7%.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.890 line:84%
Once interest
rates go up, people

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.950 line:84%
will not be able to pay for
these inflationary prices

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.740 line:84%
for cars, or major
appliances, or homes.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.620 line:84%
They'll stop buying, and
then we'll have a recession.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.540 line:84%
We're also in the
middle of something

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.340 line:84%
I don't think any American
has ever seen before,

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.160 line:90%
and that is a new woke movement.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.350 line:84%
What wokeness says
is, according to one

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.750 line:84%
of its architects,
Professor Kendi,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.200 line:84%
and to the creators of the
Black Lives Matter movement,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.750 line:84%
is simply this-- because
of discrimination

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.880 line:84%
in the history of
the United States,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.410 line:90%
it really can't be saved.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.155 line:84%
As Professor Kendi said,
to stop discrimination,

00:01:46.155 --> 00:01:47.280 line:90%
you've got to discriminate.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.190 line:84%
We now have to discriminate
by promoting people

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.560 line:84%
on the color of their
skin in proportions

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.590 line:84%
that are larger than their
percentages of the population.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.470 line:84%
As I speak, we have
people in confinement

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:02.130 line:84%
who are apparently
charged with organizing

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:04.020 line:90%
a riot or an armed insurrection.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.700 line:90%
The media told us that.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.430 line:84%
The investigatory
bodies told us that.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.870 line:84%
The Biden administration
told us that.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:11.880 line:90%
But here's the problem--

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.700 line:84%
no one has been charged
with conspiracy.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.800 line:84%
No one has been charged
with racketeering.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.740 line:84%
No one has been charged with
organizing an insurrection,

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.510 line:84%
because it was not
an insurrection,

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.760 line:90%
as the FBI has recently found.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.260 line:90%
So what am I getting at?

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.010 line:84%
I'm getting at the equal
applicability of the law

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.920 line:84%
and the administrative
state's execution of the law.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.650 line:84%
We had a 120-day riot
that had just finished,

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.500 line:90%
and that was the summer of 2020.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.660 line:84%
In 120 days of rioting, a
federal courthouse was torched,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:50.010 line:84%
a police precinct was torched
with policemen inside it,

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:53.160 line:84%
a historic St. John's
Episcopal Church

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.560 line:84%
right across from the
White House was torched.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.290 line:84%
If anything, it was called
a legitimate protest

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.390 line:84%
against the Trump
administration.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:03.390 line:84%
It was much differently
portrayed in the press

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.100 line:90%
and by the administrative state.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.910 line:84%
We've got to remember
that there is an agenda--

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.460 line:84%
an international
cosmopolitan agenda--

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.910 line:84%
by very wealthy people,
very sophisticated people,

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.230 line:90%
very educated people.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.230 line:84%
And that's something
called the Great Reset.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:24.240 line:84%
Klaus Schwab, the architect of
the Davos group who discovered,

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.540 line:84%
created, inaugurated
the idea that all

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.730 line:90%
of the world's luminaries--

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:34.320 line:84%
the best captains of industry,
the best Silicon Valley

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.220 line:84%
architects of the
internet, social media,

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.690 line:84%
the most impressive
military leaders,

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.780 line:84%
the most impressive
politicians--

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.450 line:84%
they could all assemble
at Davos, Switzerland,

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.320 line:84%
among friends, even though they
were of different countries.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.360 line:84%
They all were so
enlightened that they

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.420 line:84%
could agree that the
world was getting too hot

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.000 line:84%
and there had to be an
international body that

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.190 line:84%
overrode legislatures, or
dictators, or theocrats,

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.290 line:90%
or democracies, or republics.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.560 line:84%
This group, now,
is very earnestly

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.280 line:84%
trying to fan out through
their respective countries

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:17.940 line:84%
to harmonize all of the
nations of the world

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.720 line:84%
to turn over their sovereignty
to this select group.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.400 line:84%
In terms of globalization,
the COVID-19 pandemic

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.850 line:84%
has been an opportunity
for globalists

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.240 line:84%
to suggest that we
need more centralized

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.160 line:90%
international and global power.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.710 line:84%
We have a lot of
politicians who feel that

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.730 line:84%
under the cloak of fear
and national quarantines

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.370 line:84%
and lockdowns that they
can change the system,

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.650 line:84%
and therefore Governor
Newsom in California

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.560 line:84%
said that perhaps during
the COVID pandemic,

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.620 line:84%
we can have a more
Progressive form of capitalism

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.900 line:84%
in the manner that
Klaus Schwab said.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.080 line:84%
Hillary Clinton said, perhaps
during the COVID lockdown,

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.510 line:84%
it's an opportunity
to get a single health

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.840 line:84%
care or more ambitious
government health care plan.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.130 line:84%
I think it was Jane Fonda, the
actress and occasional Davos

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.490 line:84%
attendee, who said,
thank God for the virus

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.340 line:84%
because it was a mechanism
to get rid of Donald Trump.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.560 line:84%
We've outlined all
of the challenges

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.230 line:84%
to traditional citizenship,
but one thing is pretty clear--

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.530 line:84%
that a majority of
Americans respect and

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.110 line:84%
want to keep the
Constitution as it is,

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.360 line:84%
and they feel that they're
the luckiest people

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.850 line:84%
in the world because
they're American citizens.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.330 line:84%
As long as we remain the
majority of Americans

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.440 line:84%
and remain vigilant, the
power under our system

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.410 line:90%
is in our hands.

